@fula122You can always point out the people who are stuck on the SEC bias and can’t go beyond that to actually have a good conversation about CFB. This man said every conference is the same and the SEC is included……

No it’s not. Try telling a Texas fan in 2015 that the Big 12 that had high powered offenses and average/below average defenses was the same as the SEC or Big 10 at that point. 

Every conference has its positives and negatives that differentiate from the others. This year, it’s clear the ACC, Big 12, and SEC have better QB play than the Big 10 but you can possibly point out that the Big 10 has better defenses than the rest of CFB.

@tenebre911Yes, a rigged system produces rigged results. When draft classes and transfer portals are rigged to give extra stars to the SEC (and about eight other teams), of course more of them will start ranked, boosting the reputation of wins… and we know the cycle. 

Go watch the transfer portal. When a player moves to an SEC school, they almost always get a star added. It doesn’t get added at the end of the season, at the time they enter the portal, or at the time they are in the portal. It gets added when they see where the player signed. And it works the other way too. If a player moves from the SEC or the Big Ten to the ACC or the Big 12, they almost always get docked a star simply because of where they signed. 

Rigged system produces rigged results.

@BlvckScale yes, TN lost on the road to SC by a walk-off FG, on our 8th straight game with them off a bye, and after having THREE offensive TDs called back by penalty. 

The committee’s entire reasoning for having Tennessee below Alabama is because they aren’t in the same pod, so if you put us in the same pod, Tennessee would have to be ranked higher than Alabama. The committee is avoiding putting us in the same pod at all costs. That’s why people are angry.

There’s also only one team in CFB who has wins over two top 10 teams. That would be Tennessee. Alabama has zero.
